# MITRE ATT&CK T1021.002 — SMB/Windows Admin Shares

## ATT&CK Reference

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| Tactic | Lateral Movement |
| Technique | Remote Services |
| Sub-technique | SMB/Windows Admin Shares |
| Technique ID | T1021.002 |
| Lab Detection | DET-006 — Remote Administrative SMB Logon |
| Primary Telemetry | Windows Security Event ID 4624 |
| Supporting Telemetry | Event ID 5140 / 5145 |
| SIEM | Splunk Enterprise |
| Status | Validated |

Official MITRE ATT&CK reference:

[T1021.002 — SMB/Windows Admin Shares](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1021/002/)

---

# Technique Overview

Windows systems commonly use SMB for legitimate file sharing and remote administration.

Administrative shares such as:

```text
C$
ADMIN$
```

provide remote administrative access when valid privileged credentials are supplied.

This capability may also be used during lateral movement.

Sprint 24 focuses on:

```text
Windows Endpoint
       |
       | Privileged Authentication
       v
Remote Windows Endpoint
       |
       v
Administrative SMB Share
```

---

# ATT&CK Relationship

```text
Compromised or Authorized Account
             |
             v
