# Detection Relationship

```text
WIN11-01
      |
      v
SMB / TCP 445
      |
      v
WIN11-02
      |
      v
Event 4624
Logon Type 3
      |
      v
Splunk
      |
      v
DET-006
      |
      v
T1021.002
```

---

# Primary Telemetry

The main telemetry source is:

```text
Windows Security Event ID 4624
```

with:

```text
Logon Type 3
```

which represents a network logon.

Useful event context may include:

```text
TargetUserName
IpAddress
WorkstationName
LogonType
AuthenticationPackageName
Computer
Timestamp
```

---

# Supporting Share Telemetry

Where auditing is available:

```text
Event ID 5140
A network share was accessed
```

and:

```text
Event ID 5145
Detailed network share access
```

These can provide additional evidence of:

```text
C$
ADMIN$
```

access.

---

# Controlled Validation

Source:

```text
WIN11-01
10.10.10.101
```

Target:

```text
WIN11-02
10.10.10.102
```

Account:

```text
CORP\tadmin
```

Controlled access:

```cmd
net use \\10.10.10.102\C$ /user:CORP\tadmin *
```

Then:

```cmd
dir \\10.10.10.102\C$
```

This reproduced remote administrative SMB behavior without performing harmful actions.

---

# Positive Validation

The controlled activity generated:

```text
Successful Authentication
        |
        v
Event ID 4624
        |
        v
Logon Type 3
        |
        v
Source 10.10.10.101
        |
        v
Target WIN11-02
```

DET-006 identified the event.

```text
DET-006 TRIGGERED
```

**Result:** PASS

---

# Negative Validation

Normal/local successful authentication was generated without remote SMB administrative access.

The event did not satisfy DET-006.

```text
Successful Logon
       |
       v
Not Remote SMB Pattern
       |
       v
NO DET-006
```

**Result:** PASS

---

# ATT&CK Validation Matrix

| Behavior | Detection | ATT&CK | Result |
|---|---|---|---|
| Privileged SMB network logon | DET-006 | T1021.002 | Detected |
| Local/normal authentication | DET-006 | T1021.002 | Not Triggered |
| Administrative share access | Supporting telemetry | T1021.002 | Validated where available |
| Scheduled alert | DET-006 | T1021.002 | Triggered |

