# Threat Hunting

## Network Logons

```spl
index=* EventCode=4624 LogonType=3
```

Saved as:

```text
HUNT - Windows Network Logons
```

## Administrative Shares

```spl
index=* (EventCode=5140 OR EventCode=5145)
("C$" OR "ADMIN$")
```

Saved as:

```text
HUNT - Administrative Share Access
```

---

# Detection vs. Threat Hunting

```text
DET-006
Privileged Remote SMB Pattern
        |
        v
Alert
```

versus:

```text
HUNT
All Network Logons
+
All Admin Share Activity
        |
        v
Analyst Review
```

---

# False Positive Analysis

Legitimate causes include:

```text
IT Administration
Helpdesk Support
Software Deployment
Backup Operations
Endpoint Management
File Administration
Infrastructure Maintenance
Security Testing
```

Therefore:

```text
Remote SMB Administration
        !=
Confirmed Lateral Movement
```

---

# Confidence Model

### Low Confidence

```text
Network Logon Type 3
```

### Moderate Confidence

```text
Network Logon Type 3
        +
Privileged Account
```

### Higher Confidence

```text
Privileged Network Logon
        +
Administrative Share
```

### Stronger Correlation

```text
Privileged SMB Access
        +
PowerShell
        +
Scheduled Task
```

### High Investigative Priority

```text
Failed Authentication
        +
Privileged SMB Access
        +
Suspicious Execution
        +
Persistence
        +
Privilege Change
```

---

# Severity

DET-006 severity:

```text
HIGH
```

Rationale:

Remote administrative SMB access using a privileged account can provide substantial control over the target system.

Legitimate use remains common, so analyst validation is required.

